robosuite at 5ce6643f3092639d08f7b0f90ed1c6a84f50552c, for MuJoCo 3.17.0
(docker/RobocasaDockerfile applies it with `git apply`, which fails the build
if it no longer applies). robosuite's setup.py asks for mujoco<3.10; the image
installs 3.17.0 over that requirement and patches the two places that break:

- controllers/parts/controller.py: MuJoCo 3.10 changed mj_fullM(m, dst, qM)
  to mj_fullM(m, d, dst) (MuJoCo's changelog, 3.10.0, breaking change 14).
  env.reset() reaches this call.
- utils/binding_utils.py: under MuJoCo 3.17.0's pybind11 3 bindings,
  `mjtJoint == numpy integer` is False with the enum on the left, so
  get_joint_qpos_addr's and get_joint_qvel_addr's checks of jnt_type fail
  (the assert in env.reset()). Reading the type as a Python int compares
  equal on every version.

diff --git a/robosuite/controllers/parts/controller.py b/robosuite/controllers/parts/controller.py
index 2b3b4f58..616b1899 100644
--- a/robosuite/controllers/parts/controller.py
+++ b/robosuite/controllers/parts/controller.py
@@ -224,7 +224,7 @@ class Controller(object, metaclass=abc.ABCMeta):
             self.joint_vel = np.array(self.sim.data.qvel[self.qvel_index])
 
             mass_matrix = np.ndarray(shape=(self.sim.model.nv, self.sim.model.nv), dtype=np.float64, order="C")
-            mujoco.mj_fullM(self.sim.model._model, mass_matrix, self.sim.data.qM)
+            mujoco.mj_fullM(self.sim.model._model, self.sim.data._data, mass_matrix)
             mass_matrix = np.reshape(mass_matrix, (len(self.sim.data.qvel), len(self.sim.data.qvel)))
             self.mass_matrix = mass_matrix[self.qvel_index, :][:, self.qvel_index]
 
